  "reply_construction_scope": [
    "Logical replies are freshly constructed codec inputs, not daemon-produced replies or proof of comparison evaluation, execution, staging, durability, caps, ECANCELED/ENOENT semantics or server limits.",
    "The public MOSDOpReply constructor keeps the request READ/WRITE/RETURNVEC mode bits and replaces only ONDISK/ONNVRAM/ACK with the explicit acktype: ONDISK for success and failok, ACK|ONDISK for canceled and enoent.",
    "ACK|ONDISK on the refused vectors follows pinned PrimaryLogPG.cc: a failed do_osd_ops in a may_write vector sets update_log_only (prepare_transaction 8991-8998) and execute_ctx adds ACK|ONDISK before record_write_error (4366); a read-only refusal through complete_read_ctx adds ACK|ONDISK (9220).",
    "Per-op results follow pinned do_osd_ops stop-at-first-failure: canceled is OMAP_CMP -125 then unexecuted SETVALS 0 with aggregate -125; failok is OMAP_CMP(FAILOK) -125 then SETVALS 0 with aggregate 0; enoent is a single read-only OMAP_CMP{6b->(empty,EQ)} with aggregate and per-op -2.",
    "The enoent vector is the OMAP_CMP handler path (!obs.exists or whiteout, PrimaryLogPG.cc 7881-7885) reached with an object context present. A read-only request for an object without any object context is instead refused by do_op through OSDService::reply_op_error (PrimaryLogPG.cc 2443-2456, OSD.cc 1635-1648), which keeps only the request ACK/ONDISK bits and the request per-op results (0); that shape is not encoded here.",
    "Public claim_ops supplies input-union echoes and explicit results. Native merge_osd_op_vector_out_data independently derives payload_len 0 for every operation; OMAP_CMP and SETVALS return no output."
  ],
